    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nThis is the `26.09-alpha` version of the `main` fix: https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/8145.\nThe tag `26.09-alpha.rc2` (`cde318d`) has the bug. MLPerf DeepSeek-V3 images use this tag.\n\nFix the FC1 `out_features` of `FusedSharedExpertMLP` for tensor parallel (TP) > 1. Then TE can fuse the shared expert MLP.\n\n## The problem\n\n`_make_fused_grouped_swiglu_ops` makes the TE `GroupedLinear` op for FC1 with\n`out_features=fc1_weight.size(0) * tp_world_size`. But `fc1_weight` is the local TP shard\n(`op.weight0 = fc1_weight`), and `te.pytorch.ops.GroupedLinear` has no TP mode. So the op must use the local size.\n\nWith TP > 1, TE does not fuse GroupedLinear + ScaledSwiGLU + GroupedLinear, because\n`validate_grouped_mlp_dims` needs `fc1.out_features == 2 * fc2.in_features`.\nTE then runs the unfused ops. The unfused `ScaledSwiGLU` needs one scale for each row,\nbut the shared expert gives one unit scale. The forward pass stops with:\n\n```\ntransformer_engine/pytorch/csrc/extensions/activation.cpp:367 in function scaled_activation_compute:\nAssertion failed: scales_tensor.numel() == rows. scaled activation expects one scale per input row\n```\n\nThis problem does not occur with TP=1, because then the two sizes are equal.\nWe found it with DeepSeek-V3 on GB200: TP=2 with sequence parallel, MXFP8,\n`use_grouped_gemm_for_shared_expert=True`, and `moe_shared_expert_glu_interleave_size=32`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Use `out_features=fc1_weight.size(0)` for the FC1 op.\n- Remove the `get_pg_size` import, because it has no use now.\n- Add `test_make_fused_grouped_swiglu_ops_uses_local_shard_sizes_with_tp`.\n  The existing tests set the TP size to 1, so they did not find the problem.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/unit_tests/transformer/moe/test_shared_experts.py` on `26.09-alpha` with this fix, on one GB200 node\n  (4 GPUs): 23 tests pass. `test_shared_expert_forward_backward[2-4-alltoall]` needs 8 GPUs (TP2 x EP4),\n  so it cannot run there.\n- The new test on `26.09-alpha` without this fix fails with `assert 16 == 8`.\n- `black`, `isort`, `ruff`, and `pylint` (versions from `pyproject.toml`) pass on the two changed files.\n- End-to-end test with the same change on `26.09-alpha.rc2`:\n  - Model: a DeepSeek-V3 proxy with 19 layers and 256 experts.\n  - System: 16 GB200 nodes, TP2 PP4 VP4 EP16, MXFP8, full-iteration CUDA graph.\n  - Without the fix, warmup step 0 stops with the assertion above.\n  - With the fix, 10 training steps and the evaluation complete.\n  - The eval loss (9.698) agrees with a run that uses the non-fused shared expert (9.696).\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none. Related: #8024 makes the fused path use the TP group of the module for its collectives.\nThe two changes do not overlap. A TP > 1 run needs both if `tp_group` is not the global TP group.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] Determinism test for a changed GPU kernel: not applicable, because this PR changes no kernel.\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [ ] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
